 ## Background
-The technique of estimating surface normals via the gradient of a distance field is a fundamental concept in ray marching and implicit surface rendering [S4, unofficial]. It leverages the mathematical property that the gradient of a scalar field is perpendicular to its level sets (isosurfaces) [S2, unofficial]. The use of central finite differences for this purpose is a standard numerical analysis technique applied to SDFs [S3, unofficial]. The method is widely used in real-time ray marching shaders and offline rendering tools [S1, unofficial][S4, unofficial]. Variants using more samples (18 or 26) are discussed in the context of voxel-based SDFs [S6, unofficial]. Backpropagation-based normal estimation is a more recent development in differentiable rendering [S7, unofficial].
